**Cm $\rightarrow$ F** represents a movement from a minor chord to the target major chord (F), which fits the general concept of resolution better than the other options that either don't end on F or involve a less tense movement (Eb $\rightarrow$ F).\n\nWithout the audio, I select the option that represents a common pre-dominant to tonic movement in the key of F
