size a reaction that was likely much stronger. The speaker is sarcastically implying the person was *not* very startled when the evidence suggests they were.\n\nThe sarcasm stems from the deliberate understatement of the reaction, suggesting the person was "clearly not very startled" when the context implies they were quite startled.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{D}
